it's on App Engine?

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.496
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
Go Kit basically,

00:03:54.496 --> 00:03:57.770
it allows you to make
your services more robust.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.020
It is a micro service
framework for Go.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.310
And it manages things
like making sure

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:05.080
that you have
monitoring, and you're

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:09.220
able to instrument all your
endpoints and security,

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.250
and even things like,
well, if a server is down,

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:15.052
you should not keep on trying to
send requests all of the time.

00:04:15.052 --> 00:04:17.260
So, like, [INAUDIBLE] backoff
and all of these things

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:18.730
that you need to
take care of when

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.599
you're writing a
robust architecture

00:04:20.599 --> 00:04:22.130
with micro services.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.310
All of those things are
available in Go Kit.

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:27.160
Now, the problem is that App
Engine has some limitations

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.340
on what you can do.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:31.390
And one of them is actually
how you get an HTTP connection

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:32.320
